        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maurice Blanchot, Georges Simenon\n- Works: The Absence of the Book, The Infinite Conversation, Jules Maigret\n- Roles: writer, philosopher, literary theorist, detective\n\nFacts:\n- Georges Simenon was born on 13 February 1903 and died on 4 September 1989.\n- Maurice Blanchot was born on 22 September 1907 and died on 20 February 2003.\n- Georges Simenon was a Belgian writer.\n- Maurice Blanchot was a French writer, philosopher, and literary theorist.\n- Georges Simenon published nearly 500 novels and numerous short works.\n- Georges Simenon is best known as the creator of the fictional detective Jules Maigret.\n- Maurice Blanchot wrote the essay \"The Absence of the Book.\"\n- \"The Absence of the Book\" appeared in Maurice Blanchot's 1993 collection \"The Infinite Conversation.\"",
